From 8cb88dd8a62c0d3cfb9c91de4d3a9e9cc2247356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:57:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 51/54] streaming: count meshes waiting for upload against the
 mesh jobs

Hypothesis: the spike that gets the game killed is finished meshes. At 2 ms of uploads a frame a slow GPU takes
about one mesh a frame, the workers finish them faster during a burst of new chunks, and nothing bounds
pending_uploads: on an R36S the meshes were 12 to 24 MiB of the peak after a teleport.

Change: on a machine with little RAM a worker queues one mesh job per 128 MiB of RAM rather than 32, and meshes
waiting for upload count against those jobs. With plenty of RAM nothing changes.

Number: finished meshes' share of the peak after a teleport on an R36S, 12-24 MiB to 2-7 MiB, together with the next patch.

Falsifier: chunks take visibly longer to appear; they should arrive at the rate the uploads take them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
